Example 1.2.4. Let \(a, b, c, d, e\) be non-negative real numbers such that \(a+b+c+d+e=1\). Prove that
\[
\begin{array}{c}
a(a-b)(a-c)(a-d)(a-e)+b(b-a)(b-c)(b-d)(b-e)+c(c-a)(c-b)(c-d)(c-e)+ \\
+d(d-a)(d-b)(d-c)(d-e)+e(e-a)(e-b)(e-c)(e-d) \geq \frac{-1}{4320}
\end{array}
\]

14. Given the function $f(x)=\cos x+m\left(x+\frac{\pi}{2}\right) \sin x$, where $m \leqslant 1$.
(1) Discuss the number of zeros of $f(x)$ in the interval $(-\pi, 0)$;
(2) If there exists $t>0$, such that for $x \in\left(-\frac{\pi}{2}-t,-\frac{\pi}{2}\right)$, we always have $|f(x)|<-2 x-\pi$, find the minimum value of $m$ that satisfies this condition.

22. Given the function $f(x)=a x-1-\ln x(a \in \mathbf{R})$.
(1) Discuss the number of extremum points of $f(x)$ within its domain;
(2) If the function $f(x)$ has an extremum at $x=1$, and for any $x \in(0,+\infty), f(x) \geqslant b x-2$ always holds, find the range of the real number $b$;
(3) When $x>y>\mathrm{e}-1$, prove: $\mathrm{e}^{x-y}>\frac{\ln (x+1)}{\ln (y+1)}$.
